Set the module-level settings: which DNS provider hosts your domain,
the credential olr uses to prove the domain is yours, and who the
certificate authority should contact.

The domain itself is not set here. Published names live under the same
suffix as every other local name, which belongs to the dns module:
`olr dns set --local-domain <your domain>`.

Usage:
  olr ingress set [flags]

Flags:
      --email string                          contact address for certificate-expiry warnings
  -h, --help                                  help for set
      --no-raw-caddyfile                      remove the extra Caddyfile configuration
      --provider olr ingress show providers   DNS provider hosting your domain (see olr ingress show providers)
      --raw-caddyfile string                  extra Caddyfile configuration, appended verbatim
      --resolver stringArray                  public resolver for the certificate propagation check, repeatable (default 1.1.1.1 and 9.9.9.9)
      --token string                          provider API credential. Prefer --token-file: a value here is recorded in your shell history
      --token-file string                     read the provider API credential from a file, or from standard input when given -

Global Flags:
      --dry-run         show what would change and exit without applying it
  -o, --output string   output format: text|json (default "text")
      --socket string   olrd control socket (default "/run/olr/olrd.sock")
